cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Relational Clock Networks and Self-Timed Quantum States: a theory-first research program"
abstract: >-
  A research program testing whether temporal information in an engineered
  quantum network can be represented entirely by relations among physical
  clocks, with no privileged master clock required by the model. Theory layer
  only; no hardware run has been executed. Contains a four-run progression and
  four structural results derived at zero QPU cost and supplied as executable
  verification: rate loop closure is automatic rather than contingent; a clock
  is a usable reference frame only if gcd(rate, d) = 1; relativistic time
  dilation trades local throughput for Earth-frame storage rather than
  accelerating computation, and is negligible at achievable velocities; and
  Holevo/superdense bounds require any semantic compression to be earned in the
  classical layer.
type: software
version: 0.1.0-theory
license: MIT
authors:
